      "When nothing else touches a years-old oil stain, this is the contractor-grade degreaser professional detailers and shop owners actually reach for.",
    description:
      "Terminator-HSD (Heavy-Strength Degreaser) is formulated for the exact scenario that leaves most homeowners frustrated: an oil stain that has been baked into the concrete for years, oxidized by UV exposure, and driven over so many times that it has essentially become part of the slab's surface chemistry. Where consumer degreasers rely primarily on surfactants to lift oil, Terminator-HSD includes a heavier solvent package designed to break the molecular bonds of oxidized, hardened hydrocarbons — the kind of staining you see on garage floors under a car that's been leaking for a decade or on shop floors with decades of tire and grease buildup. In our testing on a stain that had defeated three other products in this roundup, a single heavy application with a 25-30 minute dwell time (extended to overnight for the worst section) followed by aggressive scrubbing with a stiff nylon brush lifted roughly 80% of the discoloration, with a second treatment closing the gap almost completely. This is not a gentle product, and it shows in both its performance and its handling requirements: the solvent odor is noticeably stronger than anything else we tested, so we strongly recommend working outdoors or with a garage door fully open, along with chemical-resistant gloves and eye protection to avoid splashback irritation. It's also more expensive per gallon than the water-based options on this list, running $25-30 per gallon and covering roughly 250-300 square feet per treatment depending on stain severity. For homeowners with a genuinely old, deeply set stain — the kind that's been there since before you bought the house — this is the product we'd reach for first.",
